  "notes": [
    "Antenna keepout rule areas are generated directly in the board files.",
    "Switch footprint values are sanitized as KEY_XX so Specctra DSN export does not expose legend characters such as backslash to Freerouting.",
    "X3 V2 right half has eight active matrix columns R_COL0..R_COL7; R_COL8/D20 is intentionally absent.",
    "Controller protrusion tabs are aligned toward the inner joining edge: left recessed 12 mm, right recessed 17 mm.",
    "Programming tact switch uses the smaller DeviceMart 1322056 NW3-A06-B3 SMD footprint.",
    "X3 V2 uses the KC2-owned Choc V2/PG1353 bottom-side hot-swap socket plus Cherry MX 5-pin direct-solder geometry.",
    "The exact Kailh Deep Sea low-profile switch MPN and controlled drawing revision remain pending; no family name or reseller nickname is order approval.",
    "Choc V1 switch geometry, Choc V2 direct-solder pads, and MX hot-swap socket pads are intentionally excluded.",
    "The Choc socket and MX switch are mutually exclusive assembly options at every key position.",
    "X3 V2 uses the fixed 70-key v5 no-stabilizer layout: 31 left keys and 39 right keys, with no key wider than 1.75U.",
    "X3 V2 insets every non-controller key-field edge 1.5 mm from the nominal switch-cell perimeter. Rows 0-3 use 8.025 mm center-to-edge offsets on both sides; bottom Space-B uses 15.16875 mm left / 8.02500 mm right.",
    "X3 V2 contains no legacy H1-H9 or REG1-REG9 key-field through-holes.",
    "BAT_LEAD_SLOT1 is retained as a netless copper-free strain-relief slot; the 301230 battery remains above the carrier beneath socketed U1.",
    "X3 V2 places the 301230 battery beneath socketed U1 and mirrors POWER then RESET from each USB-facing edge. J_BAT1 direct-solders insulated leads, SW_PWR1 switches BAT+ into U1 RAW/NN_B+, and B- remains on local GND. Physical stack, service, and RF validation are pending.",
    "X3 V2 uses the exact Diodes Incorporated 1N4148W-13-F SOD-123 on B.Cu with a KC2 enlarged hand-solder land: 1.40 x 1.55 mm pads, 2.20 mm inner gap, pin 1 cathode to row and pin 2 anode to the per-key switch net.",
    "The 1N4148W placements and rotations preserve at least 1.30 mm to Edge.Cuts, 1.00 mm to switch copper/unused NPTH/unrelated exposed copper, and one unobstructed 1.50 mm cardinal hand-solder approach per pad.",
    "X3 V2 uses the selected 8-left / 9-right M1.4 retention prototype: 1.60 mm copper-free NPTHs, keycaps removed and switches installed for PH0 service. Physical pilot, torque, full-pattern fit, and deflection evidence remain pending; the board is not order-ready."
  ]
